$ ./client localhost 8080 "Message 1"
Echo: Message 1
$ ./client localhost 8080 ""
Echo: 
$ ./client localhost 8080 "Hello server"
Echo: Hello server
$ ./client localhost 8080 "Message 4 with numbers 12345"
Echo: Message 4 with numbers 12345
$ ./client localhost 8080 "spaces    in    it"
Echo: spaces    in    it
$ ./client localhost 8080 "special !@#$%^&*()"
Echo: special !@#$%^&*()
$ ./client localhost 8080 "AAAA...(1500 A's)"
Echo: AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA
$ ./client localhost 8080 "line one\nline two\nline three"
Echo: line one
line two
line three
$ ./client localhost 8080 "Message 9"
Echo: Message 9
$ ./client localhost 8080 "last message 10"
Echo: last message 10
--- error handling ---
$ ./client localhost abc "hi"
Invalid port: abc
$ ./client localhost 99999 "hi"
Port must be between 1 and 65535
$ ./client localhost 9999 "hi"
connect: Connection refused
$ ./client localhost $P
Usage: ./client <host> <port> <message>
--- check long message length ---
$ ./client localhost $P "<1500 A>" | wc -c
1507
